From 2f278c0e3200bdd4d618964772ba8ea0e3aa9bca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:01:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] The Inner Garden: tap blooms hold their colour; the gate
 fits a 320 px phone

Tap blooms and petal bursts ran one strong ease-out over their whole
keyframe set, so they reached the fade a third of the way in and were pale
for most of their life. They now run linear overall with an easing per
stage: open fast, hold in full colour, fade. On short phones (568 px tall)
the gate scene gives up a little height so "Enter the garden" stays on the
first screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpEhS3XnffjKP5JTdNrd3V
